    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d318">

                <pb facs="0335" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Argentina/396: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-18T22:00:00-04:00">November 18, 1942—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1754. From U. S. Commercial Company. Embassy’s 2282, November 16, 4 p.m.<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d318-f1"/> As it was not possible to give you a telegraphic
                    reply in time, we telephoned T. J. Williams to purchase the lot of platinum at
                    the price indicated, on the understanding, which he assured us was correct, that
                    if we did not purchase same it would fall into unfriendly hands.</p>
                <pb facs="0336" n="324" xml:id="pg324"/>
                <p>Please continue to cable us for instructions when further lots of this nature are
                    available on the market. [U. S. Commercial Company.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d318-f1" n="37" xml:id="d318-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it indicated that 2½ kilos of platinum were available.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
